# Clinical content is not yours to write

Exercise names, instructions, dosages, hold times, repetitions, target muscles and safety lines all
come from the physiotherapist. She owns every clinical word.

- **Never invent clinical content.** If something clinical must be added, it ships as
  `status: draft` with `reviewed_by` and `reviewed_date` left **empty**.
- **Never write a clinician's name or a review date into any file, ever.** Not as a placeholder,
  not as an example, not in a test fixture.
- **If something looks clinically wrong, flag it — do not fix it.** Report it and stop.

# Generated files are not editable

`src/data/areas.json` and `src/data/items.json` are generated by `npm run sync:content` from the
clinician's Google Sheet. Hand-editing them puts the repo out of step with the sheet, and the next
sync silently reverts the edit with no error.

**A content change is a sheet change.** The column contract is
`patient-library/docs/CONTENT-SCHEMA.md`; the clinician's own view of it is
`patient-library/docs/SHEET-GUIDE.md`, and she is working from that document right now — if you
change the pipeline, that document has to stay true.

There are currently 26 clinician-authored items, 5 published and 21 draft. That work is
irreplaceable.
